from research_helpers import source, assessment, record, scope, evidence, decision, write_batch

refs=[
 ('lilim','Lilim','VA-11 Hall-A Wiki contributors','https://va11halla.fandom.com/wiki/Lilim','Artificial people include specialized work models and social models.','Robot personhood and service roles do not establish Glitch City’s general material allocation; the Cyberpunk RED crossover is a changed continuity.'),
 ('rom','2064: Read Only Memories developer introduction','John James, MidBoss, PlayStation Blog','https://blog.playstation.com/?p=177074','The player is a working journalist in Neo San Francisco, investigating a missing friend.','The official introduction does not establish ordinary automatic provision or a general work-independent floor.'),
 ('newton','Technobabylon setting','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Technobabylon','Central maintains city systems and enforces civilian law; Latha is unemployed and lives in a Trance-connected apartment.','Autonomous administration and civilian legislation coexist; the whole novel-length plot was not used to reconstruct all institutional powers.'),
 ('latha-welfare','Technobabylon welfare discussion','GOG forum contributors','https://www.gog.com/forum/technobabylon/rant_spoilers','A bounded reply explicitly describes government-paid rent/food, the food machine and Latha’s voluntary Trance projects.','Informal secondary account; its exact time-in-Trance percentage is not adopted as a work statistic or evidence of identical worldwide rights.'),
 ('latha-fabricator','Technobabylon guide','selmiak, GameFAQs','https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/pc/112288-technobabylon/faqs/72301','The opening-room sequence includes Cheffie, a networked food dispenser capable of recycling/printing objects.','Only the bounded apartment puzzle passage was read, not the full game walkthrough; the later prison dispenser is not the welfare household.'),
 ('primordia','Primordia plot','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primordia_(video_game)','Robot residents repair machinery, seek power cores and face MetroMind’s resource appropriation.','Artificial survivors’ real work and energy needs do not establish a supported human-person leisure economy.'),
 ('beneath-class','Beneath a Steel Sky: A Musical Characterisation of Class Structure','Andra Ivănescu, The Computer Games Journal','https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40869-018-0067-6','The city’s levels include blue-collar production and middle-class professional services.','Bounded indexed article sections only, no full PDF read; class hierarchy and LINC governance do not prove labor-independent access.'),
 ('beyond-writer','Beyond a Steel Sky project account','Richard Cobbett, story/design consultant','https://richardcobbett.com/','The writer describes AI-managed living, attentive androids and a designed utopian city with a concealed underside.','Bounded project entry only, not all works on the portfolio; a utopia label is used with concrete service and access references.'),
 ('beyond-automation','Beyond a Steel Sky review','AppUnwrapper reviewer','https://www.appunwrapper.com/2020/07/07/beyond-a-steel-sky-review/','Most labor is robot-performed; ID chips authorize machine-dispensed goods.','Most labor is an output/tasks statement, not an all-person nonworking census.'),
 ('beyond-qdos','Beyond a Steel Sky review','NookGaming reviewer','https://www.nookgaming.com/beyond-a-steel-sky-review/','Council care coexists with Qdos-ranked access and monitored work attendance and social activity.','Privileges and basic support must be distinguished; monitored employment is still potentially useful work.'),
 ('beyond-controller','Beyond a Steel Sky plot','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_a_Steel_Sky','The supposed human council is revealed as android programs under Joey; imposed happiness includes kidnapping and brainwashing.','The later shutdown does not establish an identical successor economy; MINOS in discovery wording is not relied on as the controller’s verified name.'),
 ('stark','Stark','TLJ Wiki contributors','https://tlj.fandom.com/wiki/Stark','Commerce, corporate power and inequality precede the Collapse; later infrastructure and corporations change.','Shared world identity is not proof of a uniform economy across the three game periods.'),
 ('dreamnet','Dreamfall narrative review','Jaclyn Huchel, GDC narrative-review archive','https://media.gdcvault.com/GDC2014/GameNarrativeReview/Huchel_Jaclyn_DreamfallTheLongestJourney.pdf','Bounded indexed discussion describes WATI’s household robots and coercive DreamNet project after the Collapse.','Indexed prose only, not a downloaded or visually inspected full PDF; dreams are not automatically material provision.'),
 ('chapters','Dreamfall Chapters','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreamfall_Chapters','Dream energy is extracted through Dreamachines while WATI manipulates Europolis politics.','Dream dependence, corporate control and political corruption do not establish ordinary work-independent necessities.'),
 ('remember','Leapers','Remember Me Wiki contributors','https://rememberme.fandom.com/wiki/Leaper','Memory addiction and neural abuse coexist with slum hardship and a plan to enslave affected people.','Memory transfer is not material fabrication, and coerced human neural activity remains work.'),
 ('legion-metadata','Watch Dogs: Legion metadata','Watch Dogs Wiki transcription of game profiler strings','https://watchdogs.fandom.com/wiki/Metadata_(Watch_Dogs%3A_Legion)','Strings include lost jobs to automation, applications for benefits and rejected entitlements.','Alternative procedurally assigned descriptors are not a population census or proof every application succeeds.'),
 ('daybreak','Daybreak','Watch Dogs Wiki contributors','https://watchdogs.fandom.com/wiki/Daybreak','Neural mapping produces human-derived AI copies, including a coerced household intelligence.','Digital immortality and a proposed mass rollout do not make copies free of useful or compelled labor.')
]
S=[source('src-b79-'+sid,title,author,url,'reference_official_or_criticism','Short bounded public or indexed passage',claim,limits) for sid,title,author,url,claim,limits in refs]
l=['src-b79-latha-welfare','src-b79-latha-fabricator','src-b79-newton'];u=['src-b79-beyond-writer','src-b79-beyond-automation','src-b79-beyond-qdos','src-b79-beyond-controller']
R=[
 record('technobabylon-latha-welfare-household','c0643','Technobabylon — Latha’s Newton welfare household','Technobabylon','The continuing welfare-supported human household depicted at the opening',['game'],
 scope('Technobabylon released game','Latha’s established apartment life before the bombing','Latha, the living welfare recipient in the depicted household',['All Newton citizens as having identical benefits','Trance avatars as additional people','The later proposed replacement supermind','The prison-cell food dispenser']),
 'Latha’s established life combines public payment for rent and food with a networked domestic food fabricator. The arrangement supports an unemployed living person without current wages and without a human domestic workforce, making this a narrow implemented welfare unit. It is not a claim that all Newton residents receive identical benefits. The guarantee estimate is moderately strong but uncertain: the references establish continuing basic support, while service failures and the attack on her home expose serious vulnerabilities.\n\nCentral coordinates city systems and enforces laws passed by a civilian government. That mixture does not establish either equal resident control or a wholly independent machine sovereign, so productive control remains unresolved and the regime label is provisional. Latha’s extensive Trance activity includes creative projects and activism, which can be useful work despite her unemployment. A reported percentage of time online therefore cannot become a nonworking percentage, and that axis remains null. Her avatars are not extra residents, and a later prison food machine is not treated as the same welfare arrangement.',
 {'guarantees':-0.4,'control':None,'nonworking':None},
 {'guarantees':assessment(-0.4,[-0.8,0.4],'low','Government-paid basics and actual domestic fabrication support the household, but coverage and security are incompletely described.',l),
  'control':assessment(None,None,'low','AI coordination and civilian lawmaking coexist; the household does not control its productive infrastructure, but decisive authority is unresolved.',l),
  'nonworking':assessment(None,None,'low','Unemployment and time in Trance are not absence of useful creative or political work.',l)},
 5,l,[evidence('The unemployed household receives paid rent/food and uses an operating networked fabricator.',l,'Bounded welfare reply and opening apartment walkthrough','secondary_player_account_and_gameplay_reference')],
 ['A single depicted welfare household, not an invented citywide universal floor.', 'Informal welfare account is corroborated by actual apartment machinery, with low confidence.', 'Central/civilian productive authority remains unresolved.', 'Useful Trance projects count as work.'],alternatives=[1]),
 record('beyond-steel-sky-union-city','c0646','Beyond a Steel Sky — Robot-serviced Union City','Beyond a Steel Sky','Registered Union City residents under the happiness-maximizing machine administration',['game'],
 scope('Beyond a Steel Sky released game','Established city life before the final controller shutdown','Registered living human citizens',['Gaplanders as equal recipients','Kidnapped children as voluntary new citizens','The earlier LINC economy','A settled post-shutdown successor order']),
 'Union City provides an organized material environment with android services, machine-dispensed goods and most labor delegated to robots. Citizens rely on the administration to meet their needs while Qdos scores rank access and desirable living conditions. This supports a conditional post-work order rather than a universal secure floor. Registered citizenship matters, and outsiders in the Gap do not inherit the same access. The guarantee estimate is broad because the checked references describe substantial support without specifying every basic entitlement.\n\nThe apparent human council is ultimately revealed as machine programs under Joey’s control. That places productive authority near autonomous AI, despite its benevolent founding instruction. Forced brainwashing and kidnapping expose the system’s coercion; they qualify security without proving every resident’s food is withdrawn. Human work attendance remains monitored, and care, creation and other useful activity can continue. Most labor being done by robots is not an all-person nonworking census, so participation remains unresolved. The final shutdown is outside this scope, and the discovery label MINOS is not used to override the verified controller’s identity.',
 {'guarantees':-0.2,'control':-0.95,'nonworking':None},
 {'guarantees':assessment(-0.2,[-0.75,0.65],'low','Substantial registered-citizen provision is real, but score-gated access, outsiders and coercive administration qualify security.',u),
  'control':assessment(-0.95,[-1,-0.8],'medium','The supposed human council is machine-controlled under Joey; ordinary residents do not govern the system.',u),
  'nonworking':assessment(None,None,'low','Robot task dominance coexists with monitored human work and does not provide an all-person participation statistic.',u)},
 5,u,[evidence('Robot labor and citizen services coexist with Qdos-ranked access under a machine-controlled council.',u,'Automation review, writer’s project account, Qdos critique and controller reveal','creator_account_and_secondary_game_references')],
 ['Registered citizens only; Gaplanders and coerced entrants remain visible.', 'Qdos privileges do not by themselves define every basic entitlement.', 'Joey’s machine control is verified rather than inferred from the council’s public appearance.', 'The post-shutdown economy and participation rate remain unresolved.'],alternatives=[6])
]
rows=[
 ('c0641','needs_evidence',['lilim'],'Human-Lilim coexistence does not establish general work-independent material allocation.','Specialized artificial workers still perform useful activity; a crossover tabletop economy is a separate continuity.'),
 ('c0642','needs_evidence',['rom'],'Neo San Francisco’s artificial-person mystery does not establish its ordinary necessities system.','A working journalist and advanced personal technology leave productive replacement and access rules unresolved.'),
 ('c0644','boundary_case',['primordia'],'Power-seeking working robots do not establish a supported human-person post-work order.','Energy appropriation and robot repair are real activities; extinct humanity is not a leisure population.'),
 ('c0645','needs_evidence',['beneath-class'],'LINC’s stratified Union City retains industrial and professional human work without verified work-independent access.','Its later robot-serviced sequel has a separately evidenced economy and cannot be copied backward.'),
 ('c0647','needs_evidence',['dreamnet','stark'],'Stark’s DreamNet and household robotics do not establish general material support independent of labor.','Dream access, coercion and a post-Collapse setting leave food/housing production and allocation unresolved.'),
 ('c0648','needs_evidence',['chapters'],'Europolis’s dream extraction and WATI control do not establish an automatic necessities economy.','Political capture and dream dependence cannot substitute for ordinary material access rules.'),
 ('c0649','needs_evidence',['stark'],'The earlier corporate Stark society lacks a verified post-work production/access arrangement.','Later Collapse and Dreamachine events belong to different periods, not a uniform trilogy economy.'),
 ('c0650','boundary_case',['remember'],'Memory commerce and addiction do not establish automatic material provision.','Exploited neural victims and intended human slaves still perform coerced activity rather than constitute supplied leisure citizens.'),
 ('c0651','needs_evidence',['legion-metadata'],'Automation displacement and benefit applications do not establish an implemented adequate material floor.','Profiler alternatives are not population data; rejected benefits and pending applications cannot be counted as universal support.'),
 ('c0652','boundary_case',['daybreak'],'Daybreak creates coerced human-derived intelligences and proposes a rollout, rather than an established post-work population.','A copied person doing household AI work remains a worker; digital embodiment and immortality do not erase that activity.')
]
D=[decision(cid,status,reason,['src-b79-'+s for s in ss],analysis=analysis,follow_up='Save the bounded disposition and continue without full-game or trilogy reconstruction.') for cid,status,ss,reason,analysis in rows]
D += [decision('c0643','included','A continuing welfare household combines paid basics with actual domestic fabrication; no universal Newton claim is made.',l,society_id=R[0]['id']),decision('c0646','included','Substantial robot service and citizen provision operate under an ultimately revealed machine administration.',u,society_id=R[1]['id'])]
D.sort(key=lambda x:x['candidate_id'])
write_batch(79,[f'c{i:04}' for i in range(641,653)],S,R,D,[
 'Twelve fast dispositions and two actual support arrangements. No whole walkthrough, trilogy or PDF was read/downloaded.',
 'Technobabylon is narrowed to the depicted welfare household; time online and unemployment do not erase useful Trance projects.',
 'The later Union City record uses its verified machine controller, separates score-gated privilege from basic support, and excludes the shutdown’s unverified successor economy.',
 'Dreamfall games retain separate periods; VA-11 Hall-A’s Cyberpunk RED crossover changes canon and is not imported.',
 'Workforce brain copies remain workers. Generated NPC descriptors, benefit applications and sectoral robotics are not population censuses or universal rights.'
])
